\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Happy the man that finds the grace,
\par The blessing of God's chosen race,
\par The wisdom coming from above,
\par The faith that sweetly works by love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Happy beyond description he
\par Who knows: The Saviour died for me!
\par The gift unspeakable obtains,
\par And heavenly understanding gains.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Wisdom  divine! Who tells the price
\par Of wisdom's costly merchandise?
\par Wisdom to silver we prefer,
\par And gold is dross compared to her.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Her hands are filled with length of days,
\par True riches, and immortal praise,
\par Riches of Christ, on all bestowed,
\par And honour that descends from God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. To purest joys she all invites,
\par Chaste, holy, spiritual delights;
\par Her ways are ways of pleasantness,
\par And all her flowery paths are peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Happy the man who wisdom gains,
\par Thrice happy who his guest retains;
\par He owns, and shall for ever own:
\par Wisdom, and Christ, and Heaven are one.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

